<title>FRANCE: GIAT workers take plant director hostage.</title>
<headline>GIAT workers take plant director hostage.</headline>
<dateline>TOULOUSE, France 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Striking workers at the Tarbes site of state-owned armament maker GIAT-Industries were holding the plant director hostage on Thursday as part of a protest against planned lay-offs, union sources said.</p>
<p>Some 300 workers occupied the plant in the southwest of France in the Pyrenees mountains, which makes parts for the Leclerc tank. Other GIAT workers blocked a highway toll station near Toulouse to protest at 70 planned layoffs on another site.</p>
<p>The GIAT board is meeting in Paris today to discuss a restructuring plan which could include a total of 595 layoffs, according to the unions.</p>
</text>
